@baseUrl = http://localhost:5256

### ============================================================
### Auth — run first. Access token lives 15 min: re-run on 401.
### ============================================================

### Dev sign-in (Development only)
# @name dev
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/dev

### ============================================================
### Setup — run first. Safe to re-run: POSTs are find-or-create.
### ============================================================

### Artist B — in my library as Watching
# @name artistB
POST {{baseUrl}}/artists
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "platform": "Pixiv",
  "externalId": "test-artist-B",
  "profileUrl": "https://www.pixiv.net/users/test-artist-B",
  "handle": "artist_b",
  "displayName": "Artist B",
  "status": "Watching"
}

### Work 001 by artist A — A goes to the catalog only
# @name work001
POST {{baseUrl}}/works
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "platform": "Pixiv",
  "externalId": "test-work-001",
  "url": "https://www.pixiv.net/artworks/test-work-001",
  "title": "Test sunset",
  "thumbnailUrl": "https://example.com/thumb-001.jpg",
  "artist": {
    "externalId": "test-artist-A",
    "profileUrl": "https://www.pixiv.net/users/test-artist-A",
    "handle": "artist_a",
    "displayName": "Artist A"
  }
}

### Work 002 by artist B — expect artistStatus filled
# @name work002
POST {{baseUrl}}/works
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "platform": "Pixiv",
  "externalId": "test-work-002",
  "url": "https://www.pixiv.net/artworks/test-work-002",
  "artist": {
    "externalId": "test-artist-B",
    "profileUrl": "https://www.pixiv.net/users/test-artist-B"
  }
}

### Work 003 on X by artist C, Liked
# @name work003
POST {{baseUrl}}/works
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "platform": "X",
  "externalId": "test-work-003",
  "url": "https://x.com/artist_c/status/test-work-003",
  "title": "Night city",
  "status": "Liked",
  "artist": {
    "externalId": "test-artist-C",
    "profileUrl": "https://x.com/artist_c",
    "handle": "artist_c"
  }
}

### ============================================================
### AddWork
### ============================================================

### Re-save work 001 without status — expect 200, status unchanged
POST {{baseUrl}}/works
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "platform": "Pixiv",
  "externalId": "test-work-001",
  "url": "https://www.pixiv.net/artworks/test-work-001",
  "artist": {
    "externalId": "test-artist-A",
    "profileUrl": "https://www.pixiv.net/users/test-artist-A"
  }
}

### Validation — expect 400 with externalId, url, artist.externalId
POST {{baseUrl}}/works
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "platform": "Pixiv",
  "externalId": "",
  "artist": {
    "externalId": "  ",
    "profileUrl": "https://www.pixiv.net/users/x"
  }
}

### Validation — expect 400 with platform and artist
POST {{baseUrl}}/works
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "externalId": "x",
  "url": "y"
}

### Invalid enum in body — expect 400 from BadRequestExceptionHandler
POST {{baseUrl}}/works
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "platform": "Tumblr",
  "externalId": "x",
  "url": "y",
  "artist": { "externalId": "a", "profileUrl": "b" }
}

### ============================================================
### ListWorks
### ============================================================

### All — expect 3 (after a clean DB)
GET {{baseUrl}}/works
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Paging — expect 1 item, hasPrevious and hasNext both true
GET {{baseUrl}}/works?pageSize=1&page=2
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Status — expect only "Night city"
GET {{baseUrl}}/works?status=Liked
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Platform — expect only "Night city"
GET {{baseUrl}}/works?platform=X
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Search by title (case-insensitive) — expect "Night city"
GET {{baseUrl}}/works?search=NIGHT
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Search by artist handle — expect test-work-002
GET {{baseUrl}}/works?search=artist_b
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### By artist — expect only test-work-002
GET {{baseUrl}}/works?artistId={{artistB.response.body.$.artistId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Invalid enum in query — check the error message
GET {{baseUrl}}/works?status=Loved
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### ============================================================
### UpdateWorkStatus
### ============================================================

### Work 001 -> Disliked — expect newStatus: Disliked
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/works/{{work001.response.body.$.workId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Disliked"
}

### Unknown work — expect 404
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/works/00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000000dead/status
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Liked"
}

### Missing status — expect 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/works/{{work001.response.body.$.workId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### ============================================================
### GetWork
### ============================================================

### Work 002 — expect library filled, artist.status filled (artist B is in my library)
GET {{baseUrl}}/works/{{work002.response.body.$.workId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Work 001 — expect artist.status: null (artist A is catalog-only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/works/{{work001.response.body.$.workId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Unknown work — expect 404 "Work not found"
GET {{baseUrl}}/works/00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000000dead
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### ============================================================
### LookupWork — always 200; work/artist are null when not in my library
### ============================================================

### Saved work by artist B — expect work and artist both filled
GET {{baseUrl}}/works/lookup?platform=Pixiv&externalId=test-work-002&artistExternalId=test-artist-B
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### New work by followed artist B — expect work: null, artist filled
GET {{baseUrl}}/works/lookup?platform=Pixiv&externalId=test-work-999&artistExternalId=test-artist-B
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Saved work by catalog-only artist A — expect work filled, artist: null
GET {{baseUrl}}/works/lookup?platform=Pixiv&externalId=test-work-001&artistExternalId=test-artist-A
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Without artistExternalId — expect artist: null
GET {{baseUrl}}/works/lookup?platform=Pixiv&externalId=test-work-002
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Same externalId on another platform — expect work: null, artist: null
GET {{baseUrl}}/works/lookup?platform=X&externalId=test-work-002&artistExternalId=test-artist-B
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Validation — expect 400 with platform and externalId
GET {{baseUrl}}/works/lookup?externalId=
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### ============================================================
### DeleteWork — run last. Re-run Setup to restore the deleted entry.
### ============================================================

### Delete work 003 from my library — expect 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/works/{{work003.response.body.$.workId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Work 003 still in the catalog — expect 200 with library: null
GET {{baseUrl}}/works/{{work003.response.body.$.workId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Not in my library anymore — expect only 2 works
GET {{baseUrl}}/works
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Delete again — expect 404 "not found in your library"
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/works/{{work003.response.body.$.workId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{dev.response.body.$.accessToken}}
